From b0eb9f10937f8fe96dcfcc6ebdd07ac0074bed6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sam <sam@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:25:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sqlite): node-sqlite3-wasm backend - the native sqlite3
 dependency is removed

core's SQLite usage (devdata, autocomplete cache, refresh index, docs)
now goes through core/util/sqliteBackend.ts backed by
node-sqlite3-wasm (pure WASM, installed from the npm registry) - the
native sqlite3 driver and its GitHub-hosted binaries are no longer used
at all. On locked corporate machines, npm install in core now completes
with ONLY the npm registry.

- openDatabase() returns a unified promise-based surface (run/get/all/
  exec/prepare/close) normalizing the raw-driver lastID onto run results
- the raw-driver callback/serialize usage (LanceDbIndex, ChunkCodebaseIndex
  transactions) is rewritten on the promise API so the WASM backend works
- sqlite3 + sqlite removed from dependencies entirely; dbinfoz (token
  stats, pulls sqlite3) removed as well - npm install never aborts on it
- the deprecated @database context provider no longer imports dbinfoz at
  module load: dbinfoz pulled sqlite3 and its native binding, which made
  the packaged VSIX fail at activation with "Could not locate the bindings
  file" (node_sqlite3.node is not shipped). The provider stays registered
  and returns a deprecation notice instead
- node-sqlite3-wasm added to core/cli/vscode deps; CLI bundle marks it
  external (its .wasm loads from the real module dir), vscode esbuild
  marks it external + prepackage copies it into out/node_modules
- built-in Node search replaces the ripgrep binary dependency in the
  VSIX (rg-shaped output); prepackage validation updated accordingly
---
